Package: @@PACKAGE_NAME@@
Version: @@VERSION@@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: @@ARCH@@
Depends: fontconfig, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libegl1, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxkbcommon-x11-0, zlib1g
Recommends: libgl1-mesa-dri, adwaita-icon-theme-full | yaru-icon-theme
Maintainer: Heddle contributors
Homepage: https://github.com/nikolaypaskov/heddle#readme
Description: Heddle, a de-commercialized terminal
 Heddle is a Rust-based GUI terminal with no account, no telemetry and no
 cloud services. It is an AGPL-3.0 fork of the Warp terminal with every
 first-party Warp endpoint removed: history, settings and sessions stay on
 the machine it runs on.
 .
 The built-in AI agent is not functional -- it was designed to talk to a
 server this build has no address for. Command-line agents such as Claude
 Code, Codex and Gemini CLI run as ordinary programs and are unaffected.
